@*  ============================================================
    AUTHOR: PlantSafety Platform
    CREATED: 2026-07-14
    FILE DESCRIPTION: Canonical breadcrumb trail — one of the 11 non-forkable
      shared components mandated by the Platform UI Architecture Master
      Specification (Volume 0) §4. Reuses PlantSafety.UI.State.BreadcrumbItem
      (the model already populated by every page via NavigationState.SetContext)
      rather than introducing a duplicate shared-library-local type, and reuses
      the existing .ps-breadcrumb/.ps-breadcrumb-link/.ps-breadcrumb-sep/
      .ps-breadcrumb-current classes already rendered inline by TopBar.razor —
      this component is a drop-in replacement for that inline markup.
      Pure/stateless/parameter-driven per UI001-UI005 — uses declarative
      anchors, not imperative navigation.
    Inputs: Items (required, ordered breadcrumb segments; the final entry
      renders as the current, non-linked page)
    Outputs: none
    Accessibility: nav landmark with aria-label, current page marked
      aria-current="page" per WCAG 2.2 AA (Volume 0 §8).
    SchemaVersion: 2026.1
    Additive-only evolution — see Enterprise Architectural Rule Handbook §XI
    ============================================================ *@
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="ps-breadcrumb">
    @foreach (var crumb in Items)
    {
        if (crumb.Href is not null)
        {
            <a href="@crumb.Href" class="ps-breadcrumb-link">@crumb.Label</a>
            <span class="ps-breadcrumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span class="ps-breadcrumb-current" aria-current="page">@crumb.Label</span>
        }
    }
</nav>

@code {
    /// <summary>Ordered breadcrumb entries; the final entry represents the current page.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlantSafety.UI.State.BreadcrumbItem> Items { get; set; } = Array.Empty<PlantSafety.UI.State.BreadcrumbItem>();
}
